menu "Application control"

config APP_CONTROL_PHASE_MASK
    int "Enabled closed-loop phases (R=1, S=2, T=4)"
    range 1 7
    default 1
    help
        Bit mask of connected phases allowed to drive the DAC in normal
        closed-loop operation. Disabled phases stay at midpoint. R-only
        commissioning uses 1; all three connected sensors use 7.

config APP_CONTROL_LIMIT_MV
    int "Controller command limit in software millivolts"
    range 1 6000
    default 6000
    help
        Symmetric limit before mapping the +/-6 V software range to DAC codes.
        6000 uses the full DAC code range 0..4095. Smaller values explicitly
        restrict the actuator range; the application default has no reduced
        commissioning ceiling.
        This is a software scale, not a measurement of voltage/current at the
        coil. PR and integral share the full range without fixed reserves.

config APP_OFFSET_CAL_GPIO
    int "Active-low startup offset calibration GPIO"
    range 7 18
    default 7
    help
        Input with internal pull-up, sampled only during startup. Connect to
        ground during reset to measure and persist enabled ADC offsets.
        Enabled phases must have zero physical error. The DAC stays at midpoint
        until calibration and NVS commit finish. Release before the next reset
        to reuse the stored record. Choose an unused, board-accessible GPIO;
        MCP4922 pin conflicts are rejected at startup.

config APP_PR_TRACKING_TIME_US
    int "Anti-windup tracking time (microseconds; 0 disables)"
    range 0 10000000
    default 10000
    help
        Common post-sample tracking time for the summed PR+I output.
        Component-local corrections are disabled in this coordinator.
        The initial 10 ms
        value is provisional and must be validated with the physical plant.
        Smaller values produce stronger state correction during saturation.
        Zero reproduces the linear controller with output limiting only.

config APP_DIAG_CAPTURE_SECONDS
    int "Finite diagnostic capture duration (seconds; 0 is continuous)"
    depends on ESP_RT_DIAGNOSTICS_ENABLE
    range 0 120
    default 0
    help
        Collect one window in RAM without periodic snapshots or diagnostic
        logging. Stop ADC acquisition after this duration, leave the DAC at
        its last value, then print on Core 0. Restart to repeat. Startup logs
        remain enabled; RMS logging is controlled separately. Extra storage
        is static and bounded.

config APP_DIAG_DISABLE_RMS
    bool "Disable RMS task and telemetry capture for jitter comparison"
    default n
    help
        Omit the RMS worker and per-frame telemetry copies, preserving ADC,
        FIR/PR processing and DAC generation. Use for comparison against an
        otherwise identical finite capture with this option disabled.

config APP_RMS_LOG_ENABLE
    bool "Print RMS values to the console"
    default y
    help
        Print compensation RMS and ADC/FIR mean, total RMS and AC RMS for
        enabled phases after each 100 ms capture. Disable to isolate
        console formatting and output from telemetry capture, worker polling
        and RMS calculation, which remain unchanged. No additional persistent
        buffers are allocated by this option.

endmenu
